{"title":"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denote the greatest integer which is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb6e614cd20e8b4a4df4fabdca452ecca3be415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\pi\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the integer equal to the sum of the 100 terms shown:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf44f6000a318396595aa2656dd5696eccca65d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\textstyle\\big\\lfloor\\pi\\big\\rfloor + \\big\\lfloor\\pi+{1\\over 100}\\big\\rfloor + \\big\\lfloor\\pi+{2\\over 100}\\big\\rfloor + \\big\\lfloor\\pi+ {3\\over 100}\\big\\rfloor +\\cdots +\\big\\lfloor\\pi+{99\\over 100}\\big\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"494\" height=\"24\" /></center>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realise that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca10593e08cb708535d58045663d5ef4a4b84ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi + \\frac{85}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/33450f5b99087310399f26624b191d33992884c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b96e281382af234b80bf4333d96fe86bd3bdaf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbb1eaab6afa51b4185a5cd782c42ca80e474d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1df6fc8a678ce1182e35e9d75fb82ca0373ac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.14 + \\frac{85}{100} = 3.14 + 0.85 = 3.99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"255\" height=\"38\" />. However, using similar logic, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c05788efa94ad59deaa7d76275513c16268d7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi + \\frac{86}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> is the first that goes above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b2d57fd827ffc4a44523c58ae5524754a93f186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi + \\frac{99}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> is still below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cd01eea0945d9e6bc45dd5e71565ccab9c100b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85 - 0 + 1 = 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> of the terms are just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b43b4e2fbc820684519ef89e35d216fd49a1e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99 - 86 + 1 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> are just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc390fed0b18db0874725b3cb55ebe68115eee78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 86 \\times 3 + 14 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18dc99086c5bab84b3001c97eeb36dd8abb68349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=258 + 56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73d2b8b3d470317ea768ea277efd61d5f88cc0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{314}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC\" title=\"2020 CSMC\">2020 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063016\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 147/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4682/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,m